# The plain viewer leaves the page its gestures (mer3ly site canvas plan, P2
# parity with the sandbox). Run on any viewer page, for example
#   dataset.html?dataset=fixtures/site-repository-host-history.json
# Each gesture is a synthetic browser event through the page's listeners.
# A plain wheel over the graph stays the page's (its default is kept, so a
# real one scrolls); Ctrl or Meta zooms. One finger on empty canvas is
# withheld from the canvas and keeps its default (the page scrolls); one on
# a node drags it. Two fingers pinch-zoom.
assert snap ready == true
settle 3
click role:button Pause physics
set-zoom 1
settle 2
wheel-graph 100
settle 2
assert snap gesture == wheel kept true
assert snap wheel-use == Some(Page)
assert snap zoom == 1
wheel-graph -100 ctrl
settle 2
assert snap gesture == wheel kept false
assert snap wheel-use == Some(Zoom)
assert snap zoom >= 1.1
wheel-graph 100 meta
settle 2
assert snap gesture == wheel kept false
set-zoom 1
settle 1
pinch 2
settle 2
assert snap gesture == pinch prevented true
assert snap touch-use == Some(TwoFinger)
assert snap zoom >= 1.9
set-zoom 1
settle 1
touch-graph 4 4
settle 2
assert snap gesture == touch withheld true prevented false
assert snap touch-use == Some(Page)
click role:button Fit graph
settle 3
touch-node urn:host-dataset:mere
settle 2
assert snap gesture == touch withheld false prevented true
assert snap touch-use == Some(Drag)
log gesture receipt complete
